  "findings": [
    "OpenSourceCaptureAsync opens a fresh basis without the health callback maintained by the live provider. The default callback executes two Git commands for every EnsureAvailable.",
    "Full frozen source hashing traverses all files, including unchanged cached basis payloads. Read admission and publication each repeat availability checks.",
    "First generation adds a separate basis scan. Git result construction walks the tree again and starts per-file/per-directory commands.",
    "Final release always captures a release-key generation even when the final published source identity matches; actual A logs place 84.2 percent of release inside this recapture.",
    "The 3-result Git graph verification sample is small relative to recapture. Decoder waits, cache eviction and repeated payload decoding are absent in the measured scan samples."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Cold and warm refer to the product reader/proof cache, not OS caches. Samples are ordered, once each, and not an optimized-candidate comparison.",
    "Capsule backing bytes were reconstructed from retained result blobs after historical pin reclamation; content hashes and exact Git commit fingerprint match. Historical journal layout and physical I/O are not replayed.",
    "Private paths, receipt owner and source timestamp metadata differ. Timers and stack classification add overhead. Per-check Git command counts follow the successfully executed provider path; no process-wide OS trace was collected.",
    "The original 43.1-second CLI operation is not fully phase-profiled. Diagnostic scan timings cannot be substituted for historical wall times or used as promised savings.",
    "The individual Git command latency includes process launch, loader, Git work, scheduling and security scanning. Their separate shares and any antivirus cause are unknown.",
    "Historical LP/CO and BD/GR measurements describe different code paths and inputs. No old/new performance regression percentage is established."
  ],
  "nextOptimizationBoundaries": [
    "Scope/refine basis availability proof reuse under the exact reader lease and fixed object identity, with mutation/corruption/loss tests; do not simply cache available=true.",
    "Reuse proven unchanged manifest/content identities while preserving metadata, rename/delete/revert and frozen-generation correctness.",
    "Reuse a final sealed generation only after proving source equivalence and unchanged full pre/post seals including shutdown writes and infrastructure removal.",
    "Preserve all retained result validation, conditional original publication, independent payload proof and ownership/reclamation fences."
  ],
